  "historical_output_text": " Here are simple instructions for planting a small vegetable garden from seeds:\n\nStep 1: Choose a sunny spot in your yard. Vegetables need at least 6 hours of direct sun daily to grow well. \n\nStep 2: Pick out some vegetable seeds that interest you. Common easy veggies for beginners include tomatoes, lettuce, and beans.\n\nStep 3: Get a few seed trays or small pots to start your seeds. Fill them with seed starting soil, which is a lightweight, fluffy mix ideal for tiny seedlings.\n\nStep 4: Plant 2-3 seeds per cell or pot, covering them with a light dusting of soil. Give them room to grow without overcrowding. \n\nStep 5: Keep the soil moist but not soggy. Cover the pots with a plastic dome or plastic wrap to help them germinate faster. Remove when sprouts appear.\n\n",
